-- The minimal impure `extern fn` builtin `@13` (`impure_id`): it returns its
-- integer argument, threading memory and the allocation cursor unchanged.  It is
-- the first extern with a trusted `kind = .fn` boundary spec
-- (`ExternProofs.builtinImpureIdSpec`, all five fields proven) and a program-level
-- fault-robustness artifact (`LeanProofs/FnExternFR.lean`).
--
-- This file is the exact program of that artifact's `appliedFnExternProg` —
-- `(extern fn @13 x …) 7` — so it provides reproducible evidence that the program
-- `appliedFnExtern_FR` reasons about genuinely typechecks and runs: applying `@13`
-- dispatches it, and `impure_id 7` returns 7 (memory unchanged).
(extern fn @13 x : (int :> clean {}) -> ( (int :> clean {}) )) 7
